.SH "TAFRIGH TRANSCRIBE"
Transcribe with Wit.ai or Cohere Transcribe Arabic, or retrieve existing YouTube captions.

Inputs can be media files, folders of media files, or URLs (videos, playlists, channels; anything yt\-dlp supports). The youtube transcriber accepts only YouTube URLs and existing captions in \-\-language; it never recognizes audio.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR tafrigh transcribe [OPTIONS] <INPUT> ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-transcriber\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR
Backend to use for the entire run. Required; no automatic switching.
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-language\fR \fI<LANG>\fR
YouTube: required exact caption language (e.g. ar or en\-US); no patterns or lists. Prefers manual captions, then original automatic captions; never translates. Wit: language of the apps; detected from the tokens when omitted. Cohere: ar (the default; also handles Arabic\-English code\-switching) or en.
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-recursive\fR
Include media in subdirectories. Directory symlinks are not followed.
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Hide progress bars.
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
More logging (\-v debug, \-vv trace). RUST_LOG overrides.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for transcripts; selects tree\-to\-tree mode unless \-\-output\-mode is given.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Destination layout [default: side\-by\-side without \-o, tree\-to\-tree with \-o].
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-format\fR \fI<FORMATS>\fR
Output formats, comma\-separated: txt, srt, vtt, csv, tsv, json, all, or word\-level words\-srt, words\-vtt, words\-csv, words\-tsv, words\-json.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRall
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-words\fR
Also write word timings as <id>.words.<ext> for each chosen srt, vtt, csv, tsv or json format (one cue or row per word).
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-words\fR \fI<N>\fR
Merge segments with fewer words into the following ones (0 disables).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR1
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-uncompacted\fR
Also write uncompacted transcripts as <id>.uncompacted.<ext>.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-existing\fR
Skip items when every requested output file already exists.
.TP
\fB\-\-sample\fR \fI<N>\fR
Write a sample CSV with this many random segments; suffix its name on collisions.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR0
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-vad\fR \fI<VAD>\fR
How to find speech.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRsilero
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-chunk\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Longest chunk sent for recognition, in seconds [default: 15 for wit, 30 for cohere]. Wit allows up to 60 on dictation and 20 on speech, Cohere under 400, padding included.
.TP
\fB\-\-merge\fR
Merge consecutive speech up to \-\-max\-chunk: fewer requests and more context per request [default: on for cohere, off for wit]. Wit segments still follow its utterances; Cohere gives one segment per chunk.
.TP
\fB\-\-vad\-threshold\fR \fI<P>\fR
Speech probability threshold.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR0.5
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-speech\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Shortest speech kept, in milliseconds.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR500
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-silence\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Silence that ends a chunk, in milliseconds.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR300
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-speech\-pad\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Context kept around detected speech, in milliseconds.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR250
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pad\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Pad each chunk on both sides with this many seconds of silence (0 disables). Wit drops words that start or end right at a chunk edge.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR0.5
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pad\-noise\fR \fI<DBFS>\fR
Pad with white noise peaking at this level instead of silence (0 = full scale, as in the Python tafrigh).
.TP
\fB\-\-resend\-gaps\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Resend stretches of speech that Wit returned no words for, when at least this many seconds long (0 disables). Wit sometimes stops transcribing partway through a chunk.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR1.0
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-chunk\-error\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR
What to do when a chunk fails after all retries.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRabort
.RE
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-wit\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Wit client access tokens (repeat or comma\-separate). All apps must share a language.
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAFRIGH_WIT_TOKENS\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-rps\fR \fI<N>\fR
Request starts per second for each token.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR1.0
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-concurrency\fR \fI<N>\fR
Most concurrent requests per token; fewer run while Wit or the network seems overloaded [default: enough to keep up with \-\-wit\-rps; Wit answers at about the pace of the audio, so longer chunks need more].
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-attempts\fR \fI<N>\fR
Attempts per chunk, including the first.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR5
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-max\-audio\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Longest audio per request in seconds [default: 60 for dictation, 20 for speech].
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-endpoint\fR \fI<WIT_ENDPOINT>\fR
Wit endpoint: dictation (transcription only) or speech (also extracts intents).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRdictation
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-audio\fR \fI<WIT_AUDIO>\fR
Audio sent to Wit: opus (24 kbps, about a twelfth of WAV's size; needs an ffmpeg with libopus) or wav.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRopus
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-api\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Wit API base URL (e.g. a proxy or a local mock server).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRhttps://api.wit.ai
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wit\-api\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Wit API version, sent as the v query parameter.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR20240304
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Cohere variant to download on first use (bf16, f16, q8_0, q6_k, q5_k_m or q4_k_m), or a local .gguf file.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRq8_0
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Where the model runs: auto (this build's GPU when it works, otherwise the CPU), cpu, gpu (fail without one), or gpu:N for the Nth GPU, counting from 0.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRauto
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cohere\-batch\-size\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum chunks in a Cohere GPU batch (1–64). CPU processes one at a time.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR8
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cohere\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
CPU threads for Cohere preprocessing and inference. 0 selects automatically.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR0
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-model\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Where downloaded models are kept [default: tafrigh/models in the user cache folder, such as ~/.cache/tafrigh/models on Linux or ~/Library/Caches/tafrigh/models on macOS].
.TP
\fB\-\-yt\-dlp\-args\fR \fI<ARGS>\fR
Extra yt\-dlp arguments, e.g. "\-\-cookies cookies.txt \-\-playlist\-items 1\-10".
.TP
\fB\-\-download\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Where downloaded audio goes [default: \-o, or the current directory].
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-metadata\fR
Save yt\-dlp's metadata for each URL as <id>.info.json.
.TP
\fB\-\-yt\-dlp\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
yt\-dlp executable, needed for URL inputs.
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRyt\-dlp
.RE
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAFRIGH_YT_DLP\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ffmpeg\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
ffmpeg executable (required with \-\-transcriber wit or cohere).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRffmpeg
.RE
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAFRIGH_FFMPEG\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ffprobe\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
ffprobe executable (optional; only used for progress percentages).
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRffprobe
.RE
.RS
\fIEnvironment: \fR\fBTAFRIGH_FFPROBE\fR
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<INPUT>\fR
Files, folders or URLs to transcribe.
\fBExit status:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success
.TP
\fB1\fR
Setup, filesystem or other runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid arguments
.TP
\fB3\fR
Finished, but some inputs or items failed
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Mirror a folder of recordings
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh transcribe lectures/ \-\-transcriber wit \-r \-o transcripts \-f srt,txt \-w TOKEN
.RE
.PP
Include word\-level subtitles
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh transcribe lecture.mp3 \-\-transcriber wit \-f srt \-\-words \-w TOKEN
.RE
.PP
Transcribe on this machine with Cohere Transcribe Arabic
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh transcribe lecture.mp3 \-\-transcriber cohere \-f srt,txt
.RE
.PP
Retrieve existing Arabic captions
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh transcribe https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID \-\-transcriber youtube \-\-language ar
.RE
.SH "TAFRIGH COMPLETIONS"
Generate a completion script, or install it in the shell's user directory.

Scripts call tafrigh directly; no separate usage executable is needed. Installation prints any shell setup still required and preserves unrelated files.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR tafrigh completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
Install into this shell's user completion directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the destination and setup instructions without writing a file.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<SHELL>\fR
Shell to generate completions for.
\fBExit status:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success
.TP
\fB1\fR
Setup, filesystem or other runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid arguments
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Print a script to stdout
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh completions bash
.RE
.PP
Preview installation
.PP
.RS 4
tafrigh completions zsh \-\-install \-\-dry\-run
.RE
